{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q015_artifact_tag_not_homology\",\"answer\":\"In SCOPe 2.08, d1a14h2 (1a14 H:1–8; SUNID 343393) is a synthetic N-terminal tag, classified as l.1.1.1 in class l, Artifacts. Its fold, superfamily, and family nodes are all labeled “Tags”; these are artifact groupings, not evidence of shared biological ancestry. Similarity confined to this segment should therefore not be treated as protein homology evidence or used to transfer function or choose a biological domain template. Exclude or mask it when assessing homology. By contrast, d1a14h1 (H:9–111) is an immunoglobulin heavy-chain variable domain in family b.1.1.1 (V set), superfamily b.1.1 (Immunoglobulin), fold b.1 (Immunoglobulin-like beta-sandwich), and class b (All beta proteins). Homology assessment should concern that biological domain; a shared fold or class alone does not establish common ancestry.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"mcp__scope__get_scop_domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h1\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h1/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2/parents\"]}]}"}}
